[1mMy harness was silently testing a stale binary.[22m [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not build a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m, so it loaded the [38;5;10m.so[0m from the first [38;5;10mcargo build[0m. I only caught it because a mutation I injected produced zero failures. The harness now asserts the [38;5;10m.so[0m is newer than [38;5;10msrc/[0m, and [38;5;10mverify_all.sh[0m always builds first. If you reuse this pattern elsewhere, this is the trap.[0m[0m
